## Feature 2: Video-Based Grooming Assessment

### Data Flow

```
Crew Member (Frontend)
    ↓
Initialize Camera → Record 10 seconds
    ↓
Run MediaPipe Liveness Detection (real-time)
├─ Extract facial landmarks per frame
├─ Calculate Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR)
├─ Detect blink event
└─ Mark liveness as PASSED (if blink detected)
    ↓ (if liveness passed)
Create WebM blob → FormData
    ↓
POST /check-grooming-video (multipart/form-data)
{
  "video": File (WebM blob),
  "name": "Lavanya Singh",
  "igacode": "IGA6781",
  "base": "DEL",
  "terminal": "T1"
}
    ↓
Backend Processing:
├─ Validate file size (≤ 20MB)
├─ Save temp file
├─ Extract 10 frames (1 per second)
├─ Call Gemini with all frames
├─ Parse assessment results
├─ Upload video to GCS
└─ Return compliance status
    ↓
Display Results (same as photo)
```

### Key Components

**Frontend:** `Unified_check.tsx`
- MediaStream for camera access
- MediaRecorder for WebM encoding
- Real-time liveness loop (Eye Aspect Ratio calculation)
- 10-second forced recording duration
- Base/Terminal from localStorage

**Liveness Detection Logic:**
```
For each video frame:
├─ Get 6 landmarks per eye
├─ Calculate EAR = (distance(p2,p6) + distance(p3,p5)) / (2 × distance(p1,p4))
├─ Compare to baseline EAR
├─ If EAR < 0.8 × baseline → eyes closed (blink detected)
│
Success Criteria:
├─ Face stable (variation < 2%)
├─ Eyes visible (EAR > 0.1)
├─ At least 1 blink in 10s → Liveness PASSED
```

**Backend:** `main.py` → `check_grooming_video()`
- Receives FormData with video file
- Validates size (max 20MB)
- Calls `grooming_utils.check_grooming_from_video()`
- Extracts frames via FFmpeg/OpenCV
- Sends frames + prompt to Gemini
- Parses response via `_parse_text_to_ui()`
- Saves video to GCS

**Gemini Input:**
- 10 video frames (JPEG format)
- Same grooming prompt as photo
- Temporal analysis across frames

**Gemini Output:**
- Same structure as photo assessment
- Consolidated issues from all frames

### GCS Storage

```
Path: gs://bucket/
├─ videos/
│  └─ IGA6781_Lavanya_20251120_101500.webm (1-3 MB)
│
├─ results/2025/11/20/
│  └─ IGA6781_20251120_101500.json
│     (same structure as photo)
│
├─ crew_logs/IGA6781.jsonl (append mode)
│
└─ tickets/GROOM_20251120101500.json
```

### Performance
- Liveness detection: 10s (recording duration)
- Frame extraction: 2-3s
- Gemini analysis: 10-15s
- GCS upload: 2-5s
- **Total: ~25-30s**

